    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct, which maps by property name. The existing derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `displayName`) follow a consistent pattern: a read-only computed getter on the `Owner` model + a `readOnly` property in the OpenAPI schema. I added `contactPreference` the same way:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 new computed getter:\n   ```java\n   public String getContactPreference() {\n       boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n       return hasEmail ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 a `readOnly` `contactPreference` string property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) on the `Owner` schema, so it's generated into `OwnerDto` and auto-mapped by MapStruct from `getContactPreference()`.\n\nNo OfficeFloor wiring changes were needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwner` step already serializes the full `OwnerDto`.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) now pass, as does the rest of the suite.",
