    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- `getContactPreference()` sits alongside the existing derived getter `getCityRegion()` on `Owner` \u2014 the class already establishes \"computed, read-only property exposed on the entity\" as its pattern, so a maintainer would find this placement natural rather than surprising.\n- The logic is a single cohesive unit: one derived value, computed in one small method, with no branching spilling elsewhere. Nothing is duplicated and the class isn't being turned into a catch-all.\n- The `hasEmail` local reads cleanly and the Javadoc states the rule concisely.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition mirrors the existing sibling fields (`title`/`description`/`example`/`readOnly`), and the `enum: [EMAIL, PHONE]` accurately constrains the contract to match the method's two outputs.\n\nNo structural improvements needed.",
